{
  "name": "Get a prep brief for every new external meeting in Google Calendar",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Get a prep brief for every new external meeting in Google Calendar\n\n### How it works\nWalk into every first call prepared. When a meeting is created in your calendar, the workflow keeps the attendees whose email is not on your own domain (at most max_attendees). For each one Argorant returns the person (title, seniority, place) and the company (industry, size, location, description). Your own AI model turns that into a five-line brief: who they are, what the company does, and two questions worth asking. The brief is emailed to you with the meeting title and time.\n\nCosts: 1 credit per attendee found; company data is free.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the community node **n8n-nodes-argorant** (tested with 0.3.0 on n8n 2.46.6): Settings > Community nodes > Install. Guide: https://github.com/argorant/n8n-nodes-argorant\n2. Add an **Argorant API** credential with a key from Argorant (Settings, API keys).\n3. Set own_domain, brief_to and max_attendees in **Settings**.\n4. Add a Google Calendar credential to **New meeting** and pick the calendar; add a Gmail credential to **Email the brief**.\n5. Pick a chat model in **Chat model** (any chat model node works) and activate.\n\n### Customization\nPost the brief to your team chat, or run it only for meetings with a keyword in the title.",
        "height": 626,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 1
      },
      "id": "a1f7d6a9-a7a6-49bf-b402-f43edaaa0afd",
      "name": "Overview",
